+# Phase 9b1 Task 2 report: value defects L1, L2 and L3
+
+Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS (the concerns are findings for the controller, not doubts about the fix).
+
+Commits:
+
+* `0a055271c` Phase 9b1 Task 2: value defects L1, L2 and L3
+* `2fbfe9cba` Phase 9b1 Task 2: send to an operator receiver without a second lookup
+* the commit carrying this report and the records
+
+## What changed
+
+* **L1** (`rexx-core/src/heap.rs`, weak pass): a WeakReference whose target is not a heap handle
+  (an inline string or a small integer) is never cleared. A heap target clears as before.
+  Unit test `a_weak_reference_to_a_handle_carried_value_is_not_cleared` (`rexx-core/tests/uninit.rs`).
+* **L2** (`rexx-exec/src/value.rs`, `eval.rs`, `run/loops.rs`): `Interp::operand_number` is
+  `to_number` for an operator's receiver. It answers `NotNumeric` for a String subclass instance
+  (also through a stem's default and a variable reference), so `arith_left_operand` (binary
+  arithmetic and prefix `+`/`-`) and `header_number_body` (the DO setup `+`) reach
+  `operator_message_receiver` and send. Prefix `\` already sent first and is unchanged.
+* **L3** (`rexx-exec/src/dispatch/reqstr.rs`): `required_string_dispatch` sends `STRING` to a class
+  object as it does to an instance, so a class-side `STRING` answers `say .k`, `length(.k)` and
+  `'x' || .k`.
+* `representation_refusals.rs`: no `ALLOWED` row was owned by Task 2. The only "Task 2" was the
+  `OWNERS` entry, which is deleted.
+* Witnesses, in `rust/corpus/phase-9.txt` with their `sourceline_oracle/*.txt` (generated by the
+  module's driver on a scratch copy, counts 29, 31, 15, each equal to `wc -l`):
+  `lang/weak_reference_held_values.rex`, `lang/string_subclass_operators.rex`,
+  `lang/class_side_string.rex`.
+
+## Witnesses against the oracle
+
+Each run from a fresh scratch dir, oracle under `ulimit -v 1048576` and `timeout -k 5 20`, crate
+under `memcap 2G` and `timeout 20`, release binary built from `2fbfe9cba`. All three: oracle rc 0,
+crate rc 0, both stderr 0 bytes, stdout `cmp`-identical. Stdout read line by line:
+
+* `weak_reference_held_values`: six lines `i 1 1 1 1 1 1 <value>` for `abc`, `12346`, 30 `x`, `1.5`,
+  `sub`, `an Object`. Before the fix the crate printed `The NIL object` for the first two
+  (scout probe: `The NIL object The NIL object xxx...`).
+* `string_subclass_operators`: `plus minus times div idiv rem pow`, `pfx- pfx+ not lt 3x`,
+  `plus pfx-` (stem default), `4 -3 6 9 1` (subclass with no operator method), `sent + 0` before
+  `i 1`..`i 3`, two `sent + 0` before `j 1` `j 2`, no `k` line (setup `+` answers `pfx+`, which is
+  past 4), `done`.
+* `class_side_string`: `KS`, `2`, `xKS`, `KS`, `KS 2` (inherited), `META M1 7` (metaclass),
+  `The PLAIN class 15 The Array class`.
+
+The scout probes L1, L2 and L3 now print the oracle's lines (`abc 12346 xxx...`,
+`plus times pfx- pfx+ lt`, `KS`/`2`/`xKS`/`KS`). The debug build (`target/debug/rexx-run`) gives the
+same stdout on the three witnesses, rc 0, no assertion.
+
+**Deviation 36.** The witness comment says the dropped-value case is unspecified and that a value
+carried in the handle never clears (Deviation 36), so the witness never drops one. That consequence
+of the L1 fix is the "whether a WeakReference to one clears after the program drops its last
+reference" item of Deviation 36.
+
