+## Findings for the controller
+
+1. **The oracle clears a WeakReference to a held image-resident object.** Probe
+   `docs/superpowers/records/2026-10-14-phase-9b1/task-2/probes/weak_image_objects.rex` holds
+   `.true`, `.Array`, `.environment` and `1` in variables, references each weakly, allocates.
+   Oracle rc 0: `before 1 1 1 1`, `after 0 0 0 0`. Crate rc 0: `after 1 1 1 1`. So the oracle
+   breaks Deviation 36's "a WeakReference to a value never clears while the value is reachable"
+   for `.true` and the cached integers, and does the same to non-value objects like `.Array`. The
+   crate keeps them. I kept `.true` out of the witness for this reason. Deviation 36 (or a new
+   one) may want a line, and it may be an upstream ticket. Not mine to file.
+2. **A class-side `DEFAULTNAME` is not consulted when a class renders.** Probe
+   `.../task-2/probes/class_defaultname.rex`: `::class withname` with `::method defaultname class`
+   returning `DN`. Oracle `DN 2`, crate `The WITHNAME class 18`. Pre-existing:
+   `native_string` (`dispatch/object_protocol.rs`) sends `OBJECTNAME` only for an instance. Outside
+   this task's files, so not touched.
+3. `.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-14-phase-9b1/progress.md` was already modified when I started and is
+   not in any of my commits.
+
